{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1503625-m20-sorcerer-what-determines-a-ritual-s-rank","id":1503625,"title":"M20 Sorcerer: What Determines a Ritual's Rank?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-02-21T10:43:08-08:00","id":1503625,"title":"M20 Sorcerer: What Determines a Ritual's Rank?","content":"I must be missing something in the book so I'm hoping someone can help me out. Character creation says that you have 5 points to put into a Path. Each point lets you also select a Ritual, that can't be higher than your Path Rating, and you need a Ritual of lesser rank first to select a higher Ritual. So far so good. The game also says it encourages players and ST's to come up with their own Rituals and that the ones in the book are simply Sample Rituals. Ritual's can give one of three benefits, which I'm assuming you would select when you create the Ritual. I understand all of this. What I can not for the life of me find is, what determines a Ritual's Rank? If I wanted to create a Fortune Ritual, and use the second option for Rituals where you get extra successes equal to your Path Ability Rating, how do I determine that Ritual's Rank? As far as I can tell, you select the Aspects when you're casting the spell itself, not when creating the Ritual, as it seems like you can change the Duration and other Aspects of some of the pre-made sample Rituals.<br /> <br /> Anyone here know the answer to this and able to point to a page that I might just be somehow missing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7550-vulcan7200","name":"Vulcan7200","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-21T15:55:22-08:00","id":1503638,"title":"","content":"In effect it comes down to what the player and ST consider to be fair for the Rank. There's no hard rules, but you can use things the book provides as a guideline; in general game mechanic terms, Rituals trade an increase in casting time for a decrease in difficulty.<br /> <br /> 1. Cast a Path power as Ritual<br /> - Very simple, you take the Rank from the Path level of the power you need to achieve the Ritual effect. You can dress this up to give it a different flavor. For Fortune as example, it could be a brief Ritual to predetermine the result of the next coin flip you make at Rank 1.<br /> <br /> 2. Re-skin example Rituals<br /> - Take an existing sample Ritual and change the parameters, but not the effect values. This works for examples from other Paths as well. You could adapt Eldritch Mark from Enchanting and turn it into a Fortune Ritual to curse an object.<br /> <br /> 3. Approximate by Path level<br /> - Kind of an combination of the two above; you decide you need a new Ritual to accomplish something that is within the Path's scope, but have no other guidelines. The best you can do is going through Path levels and existing Rituals step by step and ask &quot;is this more or less powerful?&quot; to eventually arrive at a Rank.<br /> <br /> As an aside, you can balance Rituals with downsides for the caster- special costs, Tass, demerits, components and so on if you feel the power level is between any examples given in the book.<br /> <br /> That's at least how I went with it since Revised.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":27477,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","user":"voidshaper","date":". 02-21-2023, 06:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-01T09:25:08-08:00","id":1504122,"title":"","content":"Voidshaper pretty much explained it well and I agree with their assessment. I am glad they defined in detail how ritual casting works because I swear to you that in revised, I had arguments with people about how the ritual sleeper flaw worked and many refused to believe it meant that you could create a ritualized version of the path spells. They read it as you are ONLY able to use the sample rituals from the book. I tried to explain that this is absurd and the book clearly implies heavily that is not the case.<br /> <br /> Some storyteller's really need things spelled out for them because some take RAW very strictly and narrowly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24121-starcomet","user":"Starcomet","date":". 03-10-2023, 12:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24121-starcomet","name":"Starcomet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24121_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-06T04:29:48-08:00","id":1504574,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Starcomet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1503625-m20-sorcerer-what-determines-a-ritual-s-rank?p=1504122#post1504122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Voidshaper pretty much explained it well and I agree with their assessment. I am glad they defined in detail how ritual casting work because I swear to you that in revised, I had arguments with people about how the ritual sleeper flaw worked and many refused to believe it meant that you could create a ritualized version of the path spells. They read it as you are ONLY able to use the sample rituals from the book. I tried to explain that this is absurd and the book clearly implies heavily that is not the case.<br /> <br /> Some storyteller's really need things spelled out for them because some take RAW very strictly and narrowly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mage is full of people arguing that 2+2=5 just because the hyper-literal interpretation of some page says so...<br /> <br /> Is m20 sorcerer actually worth it? Compared to,say, 2nd edition sorcerer?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-07T07:58:10-08:00","id":1504759,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Is m20 sorcerer actually worth it? Compared to,say, 2nd edition sorcerer? </div> </div> </div>Personally, I prefer the STV product that <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/401413\" target=\"_blank\"><b>M20 Sorcerer</b></a> is based on: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/347222/Sorcerer-Paths-of-Power\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Sorcerer: Paths of Power</b></a>. There are a very few innovations that the former has over the latter, such as completing the separation of the dice pools from the Paths (both tie the choice of Ability to the sorcerer's Practice; but S:PoP still associates each Path with an Attribute, whereas S20 makes that something that comes from your affiliation), or the way Witnesses are handled (S:PoP increases the Difficulty of a casting if there are Witnesses, while S20 removes successes instead); but for the most part, S:PoP has a much wider scope than S20 does. <br 